[00:10.94] You give us the sands on the desert
[00:15.06] You give us the waves on the shore
[00:20.90] We take what we please from the rivers and seas
[00:26.98] And still we keep asking for more
[00:31.96] You give us the mountains and valleys
[00:36.72] You give us the trees and the air
[00:42.56] We saw and we burn and still we don't learn
[00:48.46] And it seems that nobody cares
[00:54.04] Are you the giver
[00:56.64] Who longs for the gift that you bring?
[01:05.46] How can You always be
[01:08.90] All things to all things?
[01:37.56] You give us the seasons in order
[01:41.22] To nourish and build up the land
[01:47.88] With the plow and the hoe, we make the seeds grow
[01:53.54] And still things get out of hand
[01:57.78] You give us our animal brothers
[02:04.30] The feather, the fur and the fin
[02:08.56] We trap and we train till so few remain
[02:14.92] We swear we won't do that again
[02:19.78] Are you the giver
[02:23.20] Who longs for the gift that you bring?
[02:29.76] How can You always be
[02:35.52] All things to all things?
